# L0 semantic challenge round 2: 5 frozen NON_NORMATIVE samples. Round 1 drew no NN record because its pool asked for HIGH confidence and every NN record here is MEDIUM.
1 UPHELD | A fact about when a rule file loads, reported as a gap. It prescribes no routing, so it is not an instruction-architecture rule.
2 UPHELD | A skip condition of a check; the reference-direction rule is read at its own records.
3 UPHELD | A status code inside a code sample with no accompanying rule: an illustration (C5).
4 UPHELD | A code sample; its string semantics are not stated as a rule (C5).
5 UPHELD | A code sample with example values; no rule says to use this precision or index (C5).
